## Code and documentation

The scripts, configuration files, and documentation (README.md and this LICENSE) in
this repository may be viewed, copied, and adapted for non-commercial research and
demonstration purposes, provided this notice is retained.

## Audio samples (samples/)

The audio files under `samples/` are synthetic speech, generated via zero-shot,
audio-conditioned voice cloning of prosody from StressDat (Rajčáni et al., Slovak
Academy of Sciences) — a corpus licensed for research use only. Because voice cloning
can reproduce the vocal characteristics of a real, identifiable speaker even when the
words are new, these samples may resemble the voice of a real individual who has not
consented to any use of their cloned voice beyond StressDat's own original research
license.

**The audio samples under `samples/` may NOT be used, copied, redistributed,
incorporated into any dataset or model (including as machine learning training data),
or otherwise reused for any purpose — research, commercial, or personal — without the
express prior written consent of the copyright holder.**

This restriction applies to the audio files specifically; it does not apply to the
result plots under `results/` (which contain no speech or voice content, only
aggregate statistics), or to the code and documentation described above.

To request permission for the audio samples, contact Felix Burkhardt.
